// 0.0.11 T06 std library: `map` module — map helpers.
//
// All eight helpers are schematic over K and V — the bounded polymorphism of
// 0.0.3 (resolved per call site by the compiler, never spelled by the user).
// They are VM intrinsics:
//
//     std.map.get(m, k)       // -> Result<V, string>  (Ok(V) if present, Err otherwise)
//     std.map.insert(m, k, v) // -> map<K, V>  (a fresh map; m is not mutated)
//     std.map.remove(m, k)    // -> map<K, V>  (a fresh map; m is not mutated)
//     std.map.contains(m, k)  // -> bool
//     std.map.keys(m)         // -> [K]  (insertion order)
//     std.map.values(m)       // -> [V]  (key order)
//     std.map.len(m)          // -> int
//     std.map.clone(m)        // -> map<K, V>  (deep copy)
//
// Maps are always-owned values (0.0.11 D2), so `insert`/`remove` are
// FUNCTIONAL: they consume their input map and return a fresh one — the
// PLAN D2 canonical spelling is a bare argument (`std.map.insert(m, "c",
// 3)` consumes `m`); reuse needs `std.map.insert(clone m, …)` or `move`.
// The read-only helpers (`get` / `contains` / `keys` / `values` / `len` /
// `clone`) accept a bare argument too: the read copies. `get` returns a
// `Result` so the missing-key case is a value, not a runtime crash. Keys
// are restricted to int/bool/string (D5); insertion order is preserved
// (D8).
